5. Operational Implementation Dynamics
When to deploy Guillou–Hall: Best for automated clearinghouse microservices (e.g., real-time intraday margin calibration in CCPs) requiring deterministic latency and zero pilot initialization. The metric Qn(k) can be updated recursively in O(1) time per order statistic.


When to deploy Drees–Kaufmann: Best for offline, highly robust risk model backtesting where return series exhibit localized non-stationarities or microstructure clustering that cause spurious individual spacing deviations, but where the broader empirical Hill trajectory remains stable.


