5. Detailed Step-by-Step Simulation Execution Algorithm
Phase 1: Experimental Design Space
Tail Indices (): {0.20,0.33,0.50} (ensuring finite mean and variance conditions for Expected Shortfall).


Second-Order Shape (): {-0.5,-1.0,-1.5} (controlling the speed of bias convergence).


Sample Sizes (n): n{500,1000,2000,5000}.


Target Exceedance Probability (p): p=12n ($50\%$ beyond sample maximum) and p=110n (10 beyond sample maximum).


Subsample Scaling Parameter (): $\delta = 0.75 \implies n_1 = \lfloor n^{0.75} \rfloor$.


Replication Counts: Outer Monte Carlo trials M=5,000; Inner Bootstrap replications B=500.


Nominal Confidence Level (1-): 1-=0.95 (=0.05).
Phase 2: Algorithmic Execution Loop
FOR each Model ∈ {Fréchet(γ), Burr(γ, ρ)}:
    Compute exact ground truth ES_p from Section 1 formulas.
    
    FOR replication m = 1 to M:
        1. Generate i.i.d. sample X_1, ..., X_n from Model.
        2. Sort order statistics X_{(1)} ≤ X_{(2)} ≤ ... ≤ X_{(n)}.
        3. Compute second-order estimates ρ̂ and β̂ at auxiliary threshold k_1 = ⌊ n^{0.95} ⌋:
               ρ̂ = FragaAlves_Estimator(X, k_1)
               β̂ = GomesMartins_Estimator(X, k_1, ρ̂)
               
        4. FOR each intermediate threshold k ∈ [10, n/2]:
               a. Compute MVRB tail index:
                  γ̄_k = H_{k,n} · [ 1 - (β̂ / (1 - ρ̂)) · (n/k)^ρ̂ ]
                  
               b. Compute point estimate EŜ_p^RB(k) and standard error SÊ_ln(k, p).
               
               c. Compute Log-Asymptotic CI:
                  L_log = EŜ_p^RB(k) · exp( -1.96 · SÊ_ln(k, p) )
                  U_log = EŜ_p^RB(k) · exp( +1.96 · SÊ_ln(k, p) )
                  
               d. EXECUTE INNER BOOTSTRAP:
                  Set n_1 = ⌊ n^0.75 ⌋, k_1_boot = ⌊ k · (n_1 / n)^{-2ρ̂ / (1 - 2ρ̂)} ⌋, p_1 = p · (n / n_1).
                  FOR b = 1 to B:
                      Draw resample X* of size n_1 from X with replacement.
                      Compute γ̄* and EŜ_{p_1}^{*(b)} on resample.
                      Compute studentized pivot:
                          t^{*(b)} = [ ln(EŜ_{p_1}^{*(b)}) - ln(EŜ_{p_1}^RB) ] / SÊ_ln^{*(b)}
                  
                  Extract empirical quantiles t_{0.025}^* and t_{0.975}^* from sorted {t^{*(b)}}.
                  
               e. Compute Studentized Bootstrap-t CI:
                  L_boot = EŜ_p^RB(k) · exp( - t_{0.975}^* · SÊ_ln(k, p) )
                  U_boot = EŜ_p^RB(k) · exp( - t_{0.025}^* · SÊ_ln(k, p) )
                  
               f. Store indicator hits:
                  Hit_log[m, k] = 𝕀_{ L_log ≤ ES_p ≤ U_log }
                  Hit_boot[m, k] = 𝕀_{ L_boot ≤ ES_p ≤ U_boot }
                  
    Aggregate performance metrics over all M runs.

